{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, סָפַר","hw":"סָפַר","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סָפַר</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m. secretary, scribe (</strong>𝔗 Syriac; BH <span dir=\"rtl\">סֹפֵר</span><strong>)</strong>;—emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָֽפְרָא</span> <em>the secretary</em>, Persian official, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:8\" href=\"/Ezra.4.8\">Ezr 4:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:9\" href=\"/Ezra.4.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:17\" href=\"/Ezra.4.17\">17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:23\" href=\"/Ezra.4.23\">23</a>; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">סָפַר</span> <em>the scribe</em> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:12\" href=\"/Ezra.7.12\">7:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:21\" href=\"/Ezra.7.21\">21</a>, of Ezra as learned in God’s law.","next":"BDB Aramaic, סַרְבָּל","prev":"BDB Aramaic, סְפַר"}